WEBVTT

00:00:04.608 --> 00:00:06.568
Aw, they want to go together.

00:00:06.568 --> 00:00:08.904
Can I get this one too, Mum, please?

00:00:08.904 --> 00:00:10.448
They look like father and son.

00:00:10.448 --> 00:00:12.532
More like "before" and "after."

00:00:12.532 --> 00:00:13.993
They're so filthy.

00:00:14.868 --> 00:00:16.329
[SIGHS]

00:00:16.329 --> 00:00:19.248
All right, then. Go on.

00:00:19.248 --> 00:00:22.001
Honestly, I don't know how you like those things.

00:00:22.001 --> 00:00:24.420
They're just vermin.

00:00:29.175 --> 00:00:31.010
AMELIA: Liam, we've got two rabbits!

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:32.719
LIAM: Yay!

00:00:32.719 --> 00:00:35.139
This next part might get a little bumpy,

00:00:35.139 --> 00:00:36.932
but it's actually quite fun.

00:00:36.932 --> 00:00:39.685
MOTHER: Don't touch them until they've had their shots!

00:00:39.685 --> 00:00:42.104
They probably have the plague.

00:00:42.104 --> 00:00:44.064
[BARNABAS & PETER GRUNT]

00:00:44.064 --> 00:00:47.067
I'm naming mine Monkey Boo-Boo Face.

00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:48.777
Mine's Mrs. Cottage Cheese.

00:00:48.777 --> 00:00:51.364
♪ That's not my name That's not my name ♪

00:00:51.364 --> 00:00:53.366
[PETER & BARNABAS YELL]

00:00:57.535 --> 00:00:59.079
Aren't you a good rabbit?

00:00:59.079 --> 00:01:00.789
♪ I'm the last chick standing ♪

00:01:00.789 --> 00:01:02.708
♪ Up against the wall... ♪

00:01:02.708 --> 00:01:05.211
[BOTH YELLING]

00:01:05.211 --> 00:01:07.421
Hello. Hello. Hello.

00:01:07.421 --> 00:01:09.882
[LIAM LAUGHING]

00:01:11.425 --> 00:01:13.219
This is so humiliating.

00:01:13.219 --> 00:01:15.637
Here, try this.

00:01:15.637 --> 00:01:17.306
Much better. Thanks.

00:01:17.306 --> 00:01:19.599
♪ That's not my name That's not my name ♪

00:01:19.599 --> 00:01:21.477
Uh-oh! Oh, oh, oh!

00:01:21.477 --> 00:01:23.229
[BOTH YELLING]

00:01:25.105 --> 00:01:27.900
MOTHER: Let's go, kids! We're off to Grandma's.

00:01:29.985 --> 00:01:32.279
LIAM: Won't they feel scared in the dark, Mum?

00:01:32.279 --> 00:01:35.615
MOTHER: They're animals. They don't have feelings.

00:01:35.615 --> 00:01:37.868
This is what it's like to be a pet?

00:01:37.868 --> 00:01:42.580
Ah, the kids mean well, but that mum's a real monster.

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:44.958
[GRUNTING]

00:01:44.958 --> 00:01:46.960
What do we do now?

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:48.504
We go to work.

00:01:48.504 --> 00:01:51.131
[♪♪♪]

00:01:51.131 --> 00:01:53.300
[GRUNTS, SIGHS]

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:55.177
[GRUNTING]

00:02:05.854 --> 00:02:07.398
[DOOR CREAKING]

00:02:15.906 --> 00:02:17.324
[PANTING]

00:02:17.324 --> 00:02:18.867
[QUIET CLATTERING IN DISTANCE]

00:02:22.829 --> 00:02:24.039
[SNIFFING]

00:02:24.039 --> 00:02:25.207
Hm?

00:02:25.207 --> 00:02:26.666
[GRUNTING QUIETLY]

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:34.841
Jackpot.

00:02:37.344 --> 00:02:39.430
[GASPS] [SIGHS]

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:42.349
Get a bag, son. They're always under the sink.

00:02:42.349 --> 00:02:43.683
Ah.

00:02:47.438 --> 00:02:48.814
[GRUNTS, YELLS]

00:02:51.984 --> 00:02:55.070
I-- I'll just go ahead and use the handle.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:59.158
Putting tomatoes in the fridge.

00:02:59.158 --> 00:03:00.784
And they call us animals.

00:03:00.784 --> 00:03:04.246
Ooh! Oh! I get it.

00:03:04.246 --> 00:03:06.248
You wanted to get caught.

00:03:06.248 --> 00:03:10.252
You wanted to, oof, get taken to the pet shop.

00:03:10.252 --> 00:03:15.174
You wanted to get adopted so you could take their food. Oh!

00:03:15.174 --> 00:03:17.843
This is the McGregor's garden of the city.

00:03:17.843 --> 00:03:19.803
It's how we survive out here.

00:03:19.803 --> 00:03:22.181
Really? Are they all like this?

00:03:22.181 --> 00:03:24.433
Nah. It's usually just takeout containers

00:03:24.433 --> 00:03:26.477
and a bottle of champagne they're saving

00:03:26.477 --> 00:03:29.396
for a special occasion that will never come.

00:03:29.396 --> 00:03:31.106
Oh, that's so sad.

00:03:31.106 --> 00:03:33.233
Yeah, it's really sad.

00:03:33.233 --> 00:03:36.736
Hm. Hm...

00:03:36.736 --> 00:03:39.114
Anyway, let's steal some more stuff, yeah?

00:03:39.114 --> 00:03:41.325
[♪♪♪]

00:03:44.744 --> 00:03:46.121
Whoa.

00:03:47.623 --> 00:03:49.082
Whoa.

00:03:51.293 --> 00:03:53.587
[GASPS]

00:03:53.587 --> 00:03:54.796
[SIGHS]

00:04:01.387 --> 00:04:03.138
[STEAM HISSING]

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.602
Wait, we're stealing from kids?

00:04:08.602 --> 00:04:10.479
Only the stuff they'll never eat.

00:04:10.479 --> 00:04:12.314
Why do parents put it in there?

00:04:12.314 --> 00:04:14.149
So teachers won't judge them.

00:04:14.149 --> 00:04:15.984
[GRUNTING]

00:04:15.984 --> 00:04:17.861
[GRUNTING]

00:04:21.114 --> 00:04:23.701
Mm. Mighty nice haul, son.

00:04:23.701 --> 00:04:26.119
How do we get it out of here? Job's worth nothing

00:04:26.119 --> 00:04:28.747
without a good pickup crew.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:30.583
[WHISTLES]

00:04:30.583 --> 00:04:32.209
Meet the crew.

00:04:32.209 --> 00:04:35.295
Samuel Whiskers, oldest thief in the city.

00:04:35.295 --> 00:04:36.672
They ain't even his whiskers.

00:04:36.672 --> 00:04:39.091
He stole them. Heh-heh-heh.

00:04:39.091 --> 00:04:41.343
Tom Kitten. He don't say much,

00:04:41.343 --> 00:04:43.970
but when he does, you're glad he don't say much.

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:47.349
Can we come in now? I'm freezing my catnip off.

00:04:47.349 --> 00:04:50.436
And his sister, Mittens. The brains.

00:04:50.436 --> 00:04:52.062
Always keeps us on track.

00:04:52.062 --> 00:04:54.314
Enough with the introductions. Get on with it.

00:04:54.314 --> 00:04:57.776
Eh, storage room? Second door to the right.

00:04:57.776 --> 00:04:59.945
Coatroom? Third door to the left.

00:04:59.945 --> 00:05:02.155
Bathroom? I told you to go

00:05:02.155 --> 00:05:03.365
before you came.

00:05:03.365 --> 00:05:06.159
End of the hall. Thank you.

00:05:06.159 --> 00:05:08.495
So how do we get this stuff out of here?

00:05:08.495 --> 00:05:10.247
[♪♪♪]

00:05:10.247 --> 00:05:12.082
[ALL GRUNTING]

00:05:12.082 --> 00:05:13.751
PETER: Is this really gonna work?

00:05:13.751 --> 00:05:15.127
MITTENS: A well-dressed man

00:05:15.127 --> 00:05:17.212
can get away with anything in this world.

00:05:17.212 --> 00:05:20.591
And if he's got a baby with him, he can go anywhere.

00:05:20.591 --> 00:05:23.176
Three weeks ago, we rang the opening bell

00:05:23.176 --> 00:05:24.428
at the stock exchange.

00:05:24.428 --> 00:05:26.888
[BELL CLANGING] [PEOPLE CHEERING]

00:05:26.888 --> 00:05:28.766
Why did you want to do that?

00:05:28.766 --> 00:05:30.684
Because we could.

00:05:34.187 --> 00:05:35.314
SAMUEL: Okay.

00:05:37.149 --> 00:05:39.401
Oh, Howard, where have you been?

00:05:39.401 --> 00:05:42.112
I need you to help me get rid of those filthy rabbits

00:05:42.112 --> 00:05:44.323
before the children come home.

00:05:44.323 --> 00:05:46.325
Have you gotten even shorter?

00:05:46.325 --> 00:05:47.367
[YELLS, GASPS]

00:05:47.367 --> 00:05:49.119
[ALL YELLING] [YELLS]

00:05:50.078 --> 00:05:51.830
MOTHER: You little beasts!

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.081
[ALL GRUNTING]

00:05:53.081 --> 00:05:54.708
Come on. What about all the food?

00:05:54.708 --> 00:05:56.918
We're just gonna leave it? Better to live

00:05:56.918 --> 00:05:58.754
to see another day, kid.

00:05:58.754 --> 00:06:01.256
MOTHER: I'm going to exterminate you little demons.

00:06:01.256 --> 00:06:02.424
See you. Laters.

00:06:02.424 --> 00:06:04.718
No, wait. I know how to deal

00:06:04.718 --> 00:06:06.886
with cranky humans who hate our guts.

00:06:06.886 --> 00:06:09.389
You lead her to the kitchen. I'll take care of her.

00:06:09.389 --> 00:06:11.600
You meet me back at the front door.

00:06:13.268 --> 00:06:18.440
You can't hide from me, you disgusting bags of disease.

00:06:19.817 --> 00:06:22.569
[YOWLS] [GASPING]

00:06:22.569 --> 00:06:24.571
♪ Keep our teeth ♪ Ha, ha, ha!

00:06:24.571 --> 00:06:26.114
♪ Nice and clean... ♪

00:06:26.114 --> 00:06:28.283
I'm gonna get you!

